From: Kilo <kilo@local>
Date: Sun, 3 Aug 2026 06:15:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] ipv6: use RTPROT_RA instead of RTF_ADDRCONF|RTF_DEFAULT in rt6_get_dflt_router

rt6_get_dflt_router currently requires both RTF_ADDRCONF and RTF_DEFAULT
flags to identify RA-added default routes.  After CRIU checkpoint/restore
the route protocol (RTPROT_RA) is preserved but both flags are lost:
rt6_fill_node dumps rtm_flags as 0, and ip route save/restore round-trips
the netlink message verbatim.

When ndisc_router_discovery receives a new RA, rt6_get_dflt_router
returns NULL, so the code attempts to add a new default route via
rt6_add_dflt_router.  ip6_route_add then fails with -EEXIST because the
route already exists in the FIB table, logging:

  ICMPv6: RA: ndisc_router_discovery failed to add default route

Use the protocol field (RTPROT_RA) instead of the RTF_ADDRCONF|RTF_DEFAULT
flags to identify RA-added routes.  The lookup only walks the default
(::/0) node of the table and RTPROT_RA is only assigned by the RA
machinery, so matching device, protocol and gateway is unambiguous.

Signed-off-by: Kilo <kilo@local>
---
 net/ipv6/route.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/net/ipv6/route.c b/net/ipv6/route.c
index a1b0f8e..b2c3d4f 100644
--- a/net/ipv6/route.c
+++ b/net/ipv6/route.c
@@ -4454,7 +4454,7 @@ struct fib6_info *rt6_get_dflt_router(struct net *net,
 
 		nh = rt->fib6_nh;
 		if (dev == nh->fib_nh_dev &&
-		    ((rt->fib6_flags & (RTF_ADDRCONF | RTF_DEFAULT)) == (RTF_ADDRCONF | RTF_DEFAULT)) &&
+		    rt->fib6_protocol == RTPROT_RA &&
 		    ipv6_addr_equal(&nh->fib_nh_gw6, addr))
 			break;
 	}
